json5p/anchor
description: An & path anchor between the colon and the value - a reverse edge saying where else the node lives
- >
  An **anchor** `&"<path>"` standing between the pair's colon and its value declares that the
  value ALSO lives at that path - the reverse of a pointer, authored on the target's side.
  Several bookmarks may stack, and a trailing `-` segment declares positional MEMBERSHIP in a list -
  unpositioned and additive. ANY value can be anchored - a scalar just as well as an object or
  a list. The deprecated `~key:` and `~*'...'` back-edge spellings still parse and mean the same:
- !!<format: text/x-json5p> |
  boss: &": chief" {name: 'Rex', species: 'dog'},
  nickname: &": alias" 'Rexie',                    // a scalar, anchored
  fan: &": favorites: -" &": crew: -" {name: 'Bob'}, // a member of both lists
